{
  "chapter_id": "CH012",
  "title": "Prayer Corrected",
  "sections": [
    {
      "section_id": "SEC047",
      "title": "Bavardage Is Not Prayer",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Praying all night in tongues, by itself, is not proof of effective prayer. It can become mere bavardage — fatiguing talk without discernment — rather than prayer that accomplishes anything. One speaker was told plainly: \"You just exercised bavardage,\" after a night spent praying in tongues that left him and others simply exhausted.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "SRC004846",
            "SRC004850",
            "SRC004851"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004846",
            "SRC004850",
            "SRC004851"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000001",
          "provider_handle": "p1"
        },
        {
          "text": "The honest question was raised: why does this not work for us? The answer given was direct — it does not work because believers do not do what Scripture actually instructs concerning tongues. The failure was not in the gift itself but in the gap between what was practiced and what had been taught.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "SRC004880",
            "SRC004881",
            "SRC004882"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004880",
            "SRC004881",
            "SRC004882"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000002",
          "provider_handle": "p2"
        },
        {
          "text": "Those who prayed this way were sincere, even very sincere. But sincerity was not the issue. The real problem was that they did not know — their manner of praying rested on ignorance rather than on correct knowledge of what the practice was for.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "SRC004918",
            "SRC004920",
            "SRC004921",
            "SRC004923"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004918",
            "SRC004920",
            "SRC004921",
            "SRC004923"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000003",
          "provider_handle": "p3"
        }
      ],
      "idea_refs": [
        "IDEA179",
        "IDEA182",
        "IDEA186"
      ],
      "source_refs": [
        "SRC004846",
        "SRC004850",
        "SRC004851",
        "SRC004880",
        "SRC004881",
        "SRC004882",
        "SRC004918",
        "SRC004920",
        "SRC004921",
        "SRC004923"
      ]
    },
    {
      "section_id": "SEC048",
      "title": "The Refreshing",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "One of the primary purposes of praying in tongues, as taught here, is to cool or refresh oneself. This is grounded in Isaiah 28 and in 1 Corinthians 14. The speaker also referred to an earlier passage, Isaiah chapter 26, locating a related statement in verse 3, though the connection between chapter 26 and chapter 28 at this point in the teaching remained unclear in the delivery.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "SRC004854",
            "SRC004856",
            "SRC004877",
            "SRC004879",
            "SRC006457",
            "SRC006458",
            "SRC006459"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004854",
            "SRC004856",
            "SRC004877",
            "SRC004879",
            "SRC006457",
            "SRC006458",
            "SRC006459"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [
            "UNC029"
          ],
          "paragraph_id": "P000004",
          "provider_handle": "p4"
        },
        {
          "text": "Isaiah 28:11 is cited as the specific verse, and its fulfillment is located in 1 Corinthians chapter 14, verse 21. Jude is also noted as having spoken of this courageously, in verse 20.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "SRC006318",
            "SRC006319",
            "SRC006421",
            "SRC006427",
            "SRC006428",
            "SRC004861",
            "SRC004862"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC006318",
            "SRC006319",
            "SRC006421",
            "SRC006427",
            "SRC006428",
            "SRC004861",
            "SRC004862"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000005",
          "provider_handle": "p5"
        },
        {
          "text": "Because refreshment, not exhaustion, is the purpose, the practical counsel given was short rather than prolonged: when fatigued, pray in tongues for about five minutes. This brief season brings refreshment, in contrast to all-night sessions that only produce fatigue.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "SRC004859",
            "SRC004860"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004859",
            "SRC004860"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000006",
          "provider_handle": "p6"
        },
        {
          "text": "Praying in tongues is also described as bringing peace. The teaching states that when a person prays in the Holy Ghost, peace begins — and this is described as the Spirit of God praying through the believer.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "SRC006407",
            "SRC006466",
            "SRC006469",
            "SRC006474",
            "SRC006476"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC006407",
            "SRC006466",
            "SRC006469",
            "SRC006474",
            "SRC006476"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000007",
          "provider_handle": "p7"
        }
      ],
      "idea_refs": [
        "IDEA180",
        "IDEA181",
        "IDEA237"
      ],
      "source_refs": [
        "SRC004854",
        "SRC004856",
        "SRC004877",
        "SRC004879",
        "SRC006457",
        "SRC006458",
        "SRC006459",
        "SRC006318",
        "SRC006319",
        "SRC006421",
        "SRC006427",
        "SRC006428",
        "SRC004861",
        "SRC004862",
        "SRC004859",
        "SRC004860",
        "SRC006407",
        "SRC006466",
        "SRC006469",
        "SRC006474",
        "SRC006476"
      ]
    },
    {
      "section_id": "SEC049",
      "title": "He Told Me I Was Tired",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "The speaker recounted a personal experience of this correction. He had prayed so intensely that he ended up on the ground, his voice broken from the effort. Someone saw the manner in which he had prayed.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "SRC004891",
            "SRC004893",
            "SRC004895"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004891",
            "SRC004893",
            "SRC004895"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000008",
          "provider_handle": "p8"
        },
        {
          "text": "In that state, God spoke to him directly, calling him \"my son\" and telling him he was tired. God further said that if He left him in that condition without correction, he would go on to preach a wrong doctrine.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "SRC004898",
            "SRC004899",
            "SRC004905",
            "SRC004906"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004898",
            "SRC004899",
            "SRC004905",
            "SRC004906"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000009",
          "provider_handle": "p9"
        },
        {
          "text": "Alongside this, the teaching addresses a mistaken assumption about God's location or availability in prayer. God said He had never come from somewhere else, and that He had never gone elsewhere — meaning He was not absent, waiting to be reached from a distance. The real question was whether the prayer could touch or reach Him at all, described here as reaching \"the ceiling.\" If a prayer cannot touch God, it was asked, how can it change the one who prays it?",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "SRC004909",
            "SRC004910",
            "SRC004915",
            "SRC004917"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004909",
            "SRC004910",
            "SRC004915",
            "SRC004917"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000010",
          "provider_handle": "p10"
        },
        {
          "text": "The correction given was not a rejection of sincerity. It was acknowledged: \"It's ok, you're sincere. But you're not doing it well.\" The promise attached to correction was that when it is done well, true rest follows.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "SRC006452",
            "SRC006454",
            "SRC006456"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC006452",
            "SRC006454",
            "SRC006456"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000011",
          "provider_handle": "p11"
        }
      ],
      "idea_refs": [
        "IDEA184",
        "IDEA185",
        "IDEA238"
      ],
      "source_refs": [
        "SRC004891",
        "SRC004893",
        "SRC004895",
        "SRC004898",
        "SRC004899",
